Z||000000||Got2manyfieros||11-15-2000||02:08 PM||||Anyone on here auticross their car in the New England area?  <BR>For that matter, does anyone autocross?<P>I run my 84 se untill my motor is finished for my 85 GT.<P>If I can figure out how to post a pic, I'll leave some photographic evidence of my escapades.<P>-Todd||||reg||5
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||11-15-2000||02:16 PM||||I'm not in New England but I have autocrossed once...What a HOOT !!! I DNF'd my 4cly coupe (popped the heater hose clip) but then my friend let me race his 88 quad four coupe....Ye Haw !!! There were 5 Fieros racing that day. I plan on doing it some more next summer.||||reg||14
Z||000002||ChadMan||11-15-2000||04:11 PM||||Dale, I assume you're talking about our buddy Keith's yellow 88 Coupe/HO Quad 4 conversion.  <P>Please tell us in detail about how it drove!  Have you ever driven a V6 Fiero, and if so, which did you think was quicker?  How did the Coupe handle with that lightweight aluminum 4-banger back there?||||reg||10
Z||000003||Terrible Tom||11-15-2000||06:04 PM||||I've never done it but would be interested.  As I also live in Ct., let me know when/where the next events are scheduled.<P>Thanks,<P>Terrible Tom<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ed||11-15-2000||09:04 PM||||I'm still thinking about buying a Ferrari replica with a 160hp Quad Four.  <P>I currently own an '87 GT.  <P>I took a short test drive in the "Ferrino" and liked its handling.  The engine weighs about 200# less than the V-6 and has about 20 more horsepower.  <P>I like handling over straight line acceleration so the lighter car has some advantage over boring and stroking the V-6 to 3.1 or 3.4L for me.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Got2manyfieros||11-15-2000||11:41 PM||||As for CT autocross events, <A HREF="http://www.cartct.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cartct.com</A>   This is one of the clubs, and it also has links to the other local clubs.<P>For those autocrossers out there, I bought a set of Kumho race tires for this past season (Victoracers) and they are an UNBELIEVABLE improovement, everything my car used to do well, it suddenly did much better.  <P>Also, if you are thinking of KYB shocks, forget it.  Go for the Koni's they are worth the money trust me.<P>I was wondering if anyone out there has a good solution to the understeer problem I experience while autocrossing?||||reg||1
